<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">camp duties</ansi>

At camp, every member of your company sleeps by default. Rest duties let
some of them work through the rest instead: more hands on the watch, the
kit, the pot or the forage, paid for with their own sleep.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Setting duties</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">camp duties</ansi>
  Shows each member's duty for the next rest, or the ones fixed for the
  rest that is running.

  <ansi fg="command">camp duties</ansi> [member|all] [duty]
  Gives a member at your camp a duty. <ansi fg="command">camp duties mira watch</ansi>,
  <ansi fg="command">camp duties me forage</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">camp duties all sleep</ansi>.
  With no member it is your own duty (<ansi fg="command">camp duties watch</ansi>).
  <ansi fg="command">camp duties clear</ansi> sends everyone back to sleep.

  Duties stay set from one rest to the next until you change them or
  break camp (a new camp starts with everyone asleep). They are fixed when <ansi fg="command">camp rest</ansi> begins, for the members then at the camp (anyone
  who has wandered off sleeps), and settled when it ends; a restart
  never changes them. You can't change them while resting. In the web
  client, Company > Camp has a button for each duty under each member.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The duties</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">sleep</ansi>   The default. Full rest, and the Rested buff when it ends.
  <ansi fg="command">watch</ansi>   Keeps watch. Each watcher adds a chance to spot the raiders
           (their own Camp Watch level at 25% a level, never less than 20%),
           and the chances stack: two watchers spot raiders more often than
           one. A watcher who is also your camp's watch specialist counts once.
           Bells, trip lines and incense still add to the total
           (<ansi fg="command">help campwatch</ansi>). A watcher's Fatigue rises no higher than
           75 (Ready) at the end of the rest, never to Rested.
  <ansi fg="command">tend</ansi>    Tends the company when the rest ends. Each tender has the
           surgeon's kit treat one more lasting wound, if you packed a kit
           (<ansi fg="command">help camp gear</ansi>; as always it needs a healer who knows Tend and
           has the mana), or else puts a fresh edge on one member's blades
           with a whetstone (<ansi fg="command">help sharpen</ansi>), spending one use. With neither
           there is nothing to tend and the report says so.
  <ansi fg="command">forage</ansi>  Forages for food when the rest ends: 1 find, plus 1 for every 2
           levels of the member's own Forage level (a ranger's skill). Your
           best forager forages anyway, so the duty adds nothing for them.
           Foragers share the camp's forage cooldown (<ansi fg="command">help forage</ansi>), so a
           second rest soon after finds
           nothing new, and the report says the ground is picked over.
  <ansi fg="command">cook</ansi>    Cooks one dish you know when the rest ends, from your pack and cargo,
           using that member's own Cooking rank (<ansi fg="command">help cooking</ansi>). It needs no
           lit fire, because the rest was the fire. The dish gives its meal buff
           to whoever eats it (<ansi fg="command">help cooking</ansi>). Only dishes in your recipe book are cooked (<ansi fg="command">help recipes</ansi>).
  <ansi fg="command">brew</ansi>    Alchemists only. Refills flasks from your reagents, and is
           served before the other Alchemists when reagents are short
           (<ansi fg="command">help brew</ansi>). Alchemists still brew on their own at the end of every
           rest, with or without this duty.

Anyone on a duty misses the Rested buff from that rest; a watcher also
ends no better than Ready. A rest that raiders spoil (the watch missed
them) settles no duties at all. The end of a rest lists what each duty
did. If the company is fighting when the rest ends, the tend and cook
duties are left undone. Duties are extra hands on top of the specialists, whose automatic work
(your best watch, forager, cleric and kit healer) goes on exactly as before,
so if you never set a duty nothing changes.

Duties don't change the length of the rest, the world clock, or what the
company carries beyond the forage finds and what the dishes, whetstones,
kit and reagents use.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help campwatch</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help forage</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help cooking</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help sharpen</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help camp gear</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help specialists</ansi>.

Music is not a duty. A musician who sleeps still plays the camp song as the
rest begins, and one who works a duty plays it too (<ansi fg="command">help music</ansi>).
